MediCare - Hospital Appointment and Patient Management System
--abc
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"


<h2>About MediCare</h2>

<p>
    <strong>MediCare</strong> is a web-based Hospital Appointment and Patient Management System developed using Python and Django. It provides a centralized platform for patients, doctors, and hospital administrators to manage appointments, patient records, doctor schedules, and medical information efficiently.
</p>

<h3>Project Objectives</h3>

<ul>
    <li>Provide an online platform for patients to book doctor appointments.</li>
    <li>Allow doctors to manage their schedules and view assigned appointments.</li>
    <li>Maintain patient profiles and appointment histories.</li>
    <li>Help administrators manage doctors, departments, patients, and appointments.</li>
    <li>Reduce manual paperwork and simplify hospital appointment management.</li>
    <li>Improve communication and coordination between patients and hospital staff.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Key Features</h3>

<h4>1. User Authentication</h4>
<p>
    Provides registration, login, logout, and role-based access for patients, doctors, and administrators.
</p>

<h4>2. Doctor Management</h4>
<p>
    Administrators can add doctors, manage their profiles, assign departments, and maintain doctor availability schedules.
</p>

<h4>3. Patient Management</h4>
<p>
    Patients can create profiles, update their contact details, and view their appointment history.
</p>

<h4>4. Appointment Booking</h4>
<p>
    Patients can search for doctors by specialization, view available appointment slots, and book appointments online.
</p>

<h4>5. Appointment Management</h4>
<p>
    Patients can view or cancel appointments according to hospital policies. Doctors can review their schedules and update appointment statuses.
</p>

<h4>6. Department Management</h4>
<p>
    The system organizes doctors into departments such as Cardiology, Dermatology, Orthopedics, Pediatrics, and General Medicine.
</p>

<h4>7. Appointment History</h4>
<p>
    Patients can view previous and upcoming appointments, while authorized doctors can access relevant patient information for their appointments.
</p>

<h4>8. Administrative Dashboard</h4>
<p>
    Administrators can manage users, doctors, departments, appointment records, and system activities through the Django administration interface.
</p>

<h3>Technologies Used</h3>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Python and Django</li>
    <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and Bootstrap 5</li>
    <li><strong>Database:</strong> SQLite / PostgreSQL</li>
    <li><strong>Administration:</strong> Django Admin</li>
    <li><strong>Optional API:</strong> Django REST Framework</li>
</ul>

<h3>Conclusion</h3>

<p>
    MediCare aims to simplify hospital appointment scheduling and patient management by bringing doctor information, appointment booking, patient profiles, and scheduling workflows into a single web application. It helps patients access appointment services conveniently while enabling doctors and administrators to manage hospital operations more efficiently.
</p>
--abc
